  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The messageTypes parameter of data store configurations specifies what types of API-M message (access, update) the datastore will receive.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "However it is not possible to omit this (or specify \"\"): an exception is thrown on initialisation, as the String.split returns an array of a single zero-length string if it is specified as \"\" and NPE if the parameter is omitted.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It would be useful to configure datastores that do not receive API-M messages for custom messaging implementations - eg use messaging.send(destination, message) to send a new kind of message to the new destination (datastore); without the datastore also receiving the existing API-M messages.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
